# ── llm-conformance — Provider Credentials ───────────────────────────────────
# Leave a key blank to skip that provider. Missing keys are SKIPPED, never
# errors — the harness probes whatever it can reach and reports the rest as
# "not probed" so a partial run is still a valid, publishable result.
#
# NEVER commit this file. It is in .gitignore. Commit .env.example instead.
#
# Cost note: a full v1 run is 2 probes x ~4 models x 4 providers, all with
# tiny max_tokens. Expect well under $0.10 total.
#
# ── KEY LIFECYCLE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every key may carry rotation metadata. For any KEY named FOO_API_KEY:
#
#   FOO_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=2027-03-01   rotate-by / hard expiry date (ISO)
#   FOO_API_KEY_ROTATED_AT=2026-09-10   when it was last issued   (optional)
#   FOO_API_KEY_NOTE=owner, ticket   free text                 (optional)
#
# Check status:   python3 run.py credentials
# For automation: python3 run.py credentials --json
#   exit 0 = healthy   1 = expiry not recorded   2 = rotate soon   3 = expired
#
# A key with no _EXPIRES_AT is reported as "no_expiry_set", NOT as healthy --
# unknown is not the same as fine, and treating it as fine is how rotation
# deadlines get missed. Set a review date even when the key never hard-expires.

# ── REGION / MULTI-ACCOUNT PROFILES ──────────────────────────────────────────
# A single key per provider cannot express what this project measures. P3 says
# capabilities belong to the DEPLOYMENT, and region is part of deployment
# identity — Anthropic workspaces can be per-region, Azure deployments are
# per-region by construction, Bedrock model access is granted per region.
#
# So any provider supports named profiles:
#
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...                    <- the "default" profile
#
#   ANTHROPIC_USEAST_API_KEY=...             <- profile "useast"
#   ANTHROPIC_USEAST_REGION=us-east-1
#   ANTHROPIC_USEAST_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=2027-01-01
#   ANTHROPIC_USEAST_ENDPOINT=               <- optional URL override
#   ANTHROPIC_USEAST_API_VERSION=            <- optional version override
#   ANTHROPIC_USEAST_NOTE=primary workspace
#   ANTHROPIC_USEAST_SKIP=true               <- exclude from probing entirely
#
# Each profile becomes a SEPARATE deployment with its own deployment_id — the
# credential is part of deployment identity, because different accounts really
# do differ in observed capability (Bedrock grants model access per account,
# providers gate betas per org, tiers differ). Profiles are auto-discovered;
# there is no list to register.  python3 run.py probe --profile useast
#
# WHAT DISCOVERY DOES *NOT* DO — read this before adding region keys:
#
#   Adding ANTHROPIC_<NAME>_API_KEY gives you a new CREDENTIAL. It does NOT
#   change the URL. The harness will never guess an endpoint from a region
#   string. Without an explicit _ENDPOINT, the request goes to the provider's
#   default base URL.
#
#   So if you set _REGION but not _ENDPOINT, the region is recorded as
#   "declared_only" (unverified) and flagged UNVERIFIED in reports — because
#   nothing in the network path confirms it, and recording a region the request
#   never reflected would be fabricated provenance.
#
#   Set _ENDPOINT whenever the region is a genuinely different network path.
#   If the provider is globally routed and "region" describes the WORKSPACE
#   rather than the endpoint, leave _REGION unset and use _NOTE instead — the
#   distinct credential already gives you a distinct deployment_id.
#
#   Any ANTHROPIC_*_API_KEY becomes a probe target, including ones you did not
#   mean to probe (e.g. an admin-API key). Mark those _SKIP=true.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE 1 — Direct APIs (this is what v1 probes)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Anthropic (Claude models)
#   Source:  https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#   Signup:  console.anthropic.com — requires prepaid credit, no free tier.
#   Access:  Any key works. Structured output is probed via the forced-tool
#            path, which is Anthropic's documented mechanism.
#   Format:  sk-ant-...
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
#   Region profiles (us-east-1 / europe-west1 — one per workspace):
# ANTHROPIC_USEAST_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_USEAST_REGION=us-east-1
# ANTHROPIC_USEAST_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
# ANTHROPIC_USEAST_NOTE=

# OpenAI (GPT / o-series models)
#   Source:  https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#   Signup:  platform.openai.com — requires prepaid credit, no free tier.
#   Access:  Project-scoped keys work. NOTE: strict json_schema is gated on
#            some older models — a rejection there is itself a finding, not a
#            setup problem, so probe with the key you have.
#   Format:  sk-proj-... or sk-...
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
OPENAI_API_KEY_ROTATED_AT=
OPENAI_API_KEY_NOTE=
#   Region profiles (OpenAI direct is not region-scoped; use for multi-account):
# OPENAI_USEAST_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_USEAST_REGION=us-east-1
# OPENAI_USEAST_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
# OPENAI_USEAST_NOTE=

# Google Gemini
#   Source:  https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   Signup:  Free tier available; rate-limited but sufficient for probing.
#   Access:  This is the AI Studio / Generative Language API key, which is a
#            DIFFERENT surface from Vertex AI (phase 2). Same models, different
#            platform — that gap is exactly what this project measures.
#   Format:  AIza...
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
GEMINI_API_KEY_ROTATED_AT=
GEMINI_API_KEY_NOTE=
#   Region profiles (AI Studio is not region-scoped; Vertex is (phase 2)):
# GEMINI_USEAST_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_USEAST_REGION=us-east-1
# GEMINI_USEAST_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
# GEMINI_USEAST_NOTE=

# DeepSeek
#   Source:  https://platform.deepseek.com/api_keys
#   Signup:  platform.deepseek.com — prepaid, very low cost.
#   Access:  OpenAI-compatible surface. Whether that compatibility extends to
#            strict schema enforcement is precisely the open question.
#   Format:  sk-...
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY_ROTATED_AT=
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY_NOTE=
#   Region profiles (not region-scoped today):
# DEEPSEEK_USEAST_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_USEAST_REGION=us-east-1
# DEEPSEEK_USEAST_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
# DEEPSEEK_USEAST_NOTE=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PHASE 2 — Cloud marketplaces (higher value, slower onboarding — not yet wired)
#
# These are the real targets: same model, different platform, different
# behavior. Onboarding is the cost here, not API spend. Uncomment as accounts
# come online.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Azure OpenAI
#   Source:  Azure Portal > your Azure OpenAI resource > Keys and Endpoint
#   Onboard: Requires an Azure subscription. Each model is a per-region
#            "deployment" you create yourself, so the deployment name is NOT
#            the model name — record both.
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY_EXPIRES_AT=
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://<resource>.openai.azure.com
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-10-21
#   Azure keys are rotated in pairs (key1/key2) — record which one is live in
#   _NOTE so a rotation does not become an outage.

# AWS Bedrock
#   Source:  IAM > Users > Security credentials (or use an instance role)
#   Onboard: SLOWEST PATH. Model access is request-and-approve, per model,
#            per region. Start the access requests before you need them.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID_EXPIRES_AT=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# Google Vertex AI
#   Source:  gcloud auth application-default login  (ADC — no static key)
#   Onboard: Needs a GCP project with Vertex AI API enabled + billing.
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=us-central1
